{"name":"Quarry Quartz","hex":"#af9a91","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"quarry","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A site for mining stone, such as limestone, or slate."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To obtain (or mine) stone by extraction from a quarry.","To extract or slowly obtain by long, tedious searching."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/quarry"},{"term":"quartz","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The most abundant mineral on the earth's surface, of chemical composition silicon dioxide, SiO2. It occurs in a variety of forms, both crystalline and amorphous. Found in every environment.","Crystal meth: methamphetamine hydrochloride."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/quartz"}],"entries":[{"title":"Quarry","blocks":[{"text":"A quarry is a place where rock and earth materials – such as limestone, marble, granite, gravel, and sand – are excavated. The operation of quarries is regulated in some jurisdictions to manage their safety risks and reduce their environmental impact."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2d/PortlandQuarry.jpg/330px-PortlandQuarry.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Quarry","wikidata":"Q188040"},{"title":"Quartz","blocks":[{"text":"Quartz is a hard mineral composed of silica (silicon dioxide). Its atoms are linked in a continuous framework of SiO4 silicon–oxygen tetrahedra, with each oxygen atom being shared between two tetrahedra, giving an overall chemical formula of SiO2. Therefore, quartz is classified structurally as a framework silicate mineral and compositionally as an oxide mineral. Quartz is the second most common mineral or mineral group in Earth's lithosphere, comprising about 12% by mass."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ce/Quartz_Br%C3%A9sil.jpg/330px-Quartz_Br%C3%A9sil.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=a